# The games gallery's table (dm/tools/docs_gallery.py writes README.md's gallery from it): a new game is a row at its end. README.md itself is not merged this way; after a
# conflict in its gallery, run docs_gallery.py. test_docs fails on a game in the table twice
docs/images/gallery.tsv merge=union
# Shell scripts keep LF line endings in every checkout, also on Windows with core.autocrlf: Git Bash and the Linux containers run them from a Windows checkout
# (dm/host/tests/run_host_tests.sh, docker/README.md), and a CR at a line end breaks them
*.sh text eol=lf
# The shader chain's version (DMSH_CHAIN) is a sha256 of the bytes of the files in FILES of dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_chain.py, so they keep LF line endings in every checkout, also on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true: a checkout with CRLF made dmsh_chain.py print 2aff3aff9a76 instead of the committed 157e1b96c8da, and no shader build there could match a Mac's.
# Keep these patterns covering FILES (dm/tools/tests/test_nsp_chain.py checks it)
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_*.py text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_pull.metal text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_chain.lock text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_xlate/Program.cs text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_xlate/dmsh_xlate.csproj text eol=lf
dm/ios/tools/ios_metal.py text eol=lf
dm/third_party/ryujinx/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/**/*.cs text eol=lf
# The same for the Vulkan chain's version (DMSH_CHAIN_VK, FILES of dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_chain_vk.py; dmsh_*.py above covers its Python files): the Vulkan translator's sources,
# its lock, and the two analyses the Vulkan build runs (test_nsp_chain.py checks these too)
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_xlate_vk/Program.cs text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_xlate_vk/dmsh_xlate_vk.csproj text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_chain_vk.lock text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/c1_guard.py text eol=lf
dm/gfx/tools/cb_extent.py text eol=lf
